<!--Post: 1392--><!--Time: 1099931895-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1392"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Topeka_guy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Topeka_guy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, November 08, 2004 - 8:38 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi, I&#39;ve been lurking around this forum for the past few months and enjoying reading the messages.  <BR> <BR>I&#39;d like to ask for your opinions as to whether or not you believe Kathryn Bright was killed by BTK. The M.O. sure seems the same as many of the other killings &#40;both Nancy Fox and the Anna Williams incident&#41; and I think that Kevin Bright&#39;s description could definately be BTK in disguise &#40;doesn&#39;t his description hold up with what the British psychic said was his disguise?&#41;.  <BR> <BR>Also, does anybody know if anything was taken from the Bright scene? Although if BTK were on the run as he knew Kevin Bright had escaped, perhaps he didn&#39;t have time to take pictures or artifacts from the apartment. Perhaps this accounts for his literary silence on this murder.  <BR> <BR>I believe I read elsewhere online, although I am unsure where, that BTK did claim Bright in a letter which remains unreleased to the public. This information was accidentally leaked by a psychologist or detective who had knowledge of the case. Has anyone else read this information? <BR> <BR>Your opinions, comments? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1392-->
<!--Post: 1403--><!--Time: 1099984527-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1403"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mijilu<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mijilu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, November 08, 2004 - 11:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think BTK killed Kathryn Bright. The intruder Kevin described sounded very calm, even though Kevin appearing with his sister was probably a surprise to BTK. He tried to strangle Kevin, but Kevin was a strong young man who was fighting for his life. I think he was about to be more than BTK could handle, so he shot him.  <BR> <BR>   As to BTK taking anything from the scene, remember he was in the house when they arrived home. He might have already rummaged and found something he wanted. <BR> <BR>  I, too, have read that BTK had claimed the Bright case in a letter, or portion of a letter that was not released to the public. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1403-->
<!--Post: 1438--><!--Time: 1101237297-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1438"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lisa<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lisa<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, November 23, 2004 - 11:14 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have to agree with you Mijilu.  I do believe Kathryn was BTK&#39;s victim.  I think that if she wasn&#39;t, BTK would have said so in a letter.  Since WPD seems certain Kathryn was a BTK victim, there&#39;s no doubt in my mind he wrote a letter claiming her.  He also copied off of the Zodiac when he killed her, and I think he did that to get his name in the papers.  Perhaps since he wasn&#39;t successful in killing Kevin, he didn&#39;t want it publicized, because he failed.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1438-->
<!--Post: 1471--><!--Time: 1101861593-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1471"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, November 30, 2004 - 4:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK not only failed to kill Kevin, he apparently allowed Kevin to wrestle his gun away and pull the trigger! The gun misfired and BTK eventually got it back. However, not exactly a highlight-film moment for BTK to brag about...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1471-->
<!--Post: 1502--><!--Time: 1101912784-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1502"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 01, 2004 - 6:53 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree. BTK is quite proud of himself. He really did bungle that one and I do believe that BTK killed Ms. Bright.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1502-->
<!--Post: 3166--><!--Time: 1104537640-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3166"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 31, 2004 - 4:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Is the type of hand gun known? <BR> <BR>Is there a type of hand gun that allows the trigger to be pulled part way or without firing  &#34;with the safety on&#34;... giving the impression to kevin that he pulled it but it didn&#39;t fire?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3166-->
<!--Post: 3183--><!--Time: 1104565033-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3183"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 31, 2004 - 11:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This article uses the term &#34;pistol&#34;, but it may have been used loosely to describe a revolver.  In either case it was a 22 caliber. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.kake.com/home/headlines/794962.html" target=_top>http://www.kake.com/home/headlines/794962.html</a> <BR> <BR>Several possible scenarios would fit this.  In all of them, pulling the trigger would have been useless. <BR> <BR>Either a single-action revolver with the hammer down &#40;requires the hammer to be cocked back with the thumb to advance the cylinder and raise the hammer&#41;, or a semi-auto pistol with the clip in but the bolt unretracted, or with the bolt retracted and a round chambered but the safety on.  All are good ways to carry if you want to avoid an accidental firing, but you think you&#39;ll have time to c0ck it, pull the slide, or flip the safety.  Semi-auto with round chambered and safety on is probably the best combination - fastest but safest for the shooter, IMHO.  Not sure if Kevin was a shooter, but using somebody else&#39;s gun is always a momentary challenge unless you&#39;re familiar with the model and know the state it&#39;s in when you take hold of it. <BR> <BR>My guess would be single-action revolver, if it was his 1950&#39;s &#34;growing up gun&#34;.  Common, easy to c0ck &#40;1 second&#41;, but won&#39;t fire into your thigh if you&#39;re screwing around with other activities like BTK.  Could also have been a 22 semi-auto pistol with the clip in and no round chambered &#40;unlikely for BTK, who might need speed&#41;, or a round in and the safety on.  May be all that he had.  Both are common kids&#39; first guns in a gun-owning households.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3183-->
<!--Post: 3981--><!--Time: 1105499345-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3981"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 7:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There are many odd aspcests with this murder case. One of the oddest components to it is Kevin Bright. <BR>He first told investigators that the assailant was wearing an orange shirt and an orange windbreaker. 30 years later he remembered it as wearing camouflage not orange. <BR>He worked for Coleman from March 1973 to June 1973 and then quit to take a vacation. Three months and he quits to take a vacation? He was rehired at Coleman for the same job in July but then quit again in August. <BR>Curiously also working at Coleman are his sister, murder victim Katheryn Bright and murder victim Mrs. Otero who both worked on assembly. Both murdered by allegedly the same person within less than three months of each other in early 1974. Katheryn Bright did not work as an assembler at the same time as Mrs. Otero. Bright worked as a brazer at Coleman at the time of Otero&#39;s murder and began her job on the assembly about three weeks before she herself was killed. Oddly the assembly supervisor Michael L. Williams was shot in the abdomen on January 12 two days before the Otero murders by two intruders who fired a shotgun blast through a door at him. Odder still is that on March 28 one week before Bright&#39;s murder someone broke into williams&#39; home and stole a rifle and a radio. Yet even odder still investigators were unable to lift any prints because in the meantime Williams had touched all the surface areas that the burglar had. <BR>There were reports that there was a quantity of drugs found at the Bright home. What kind of drugs and how much has never been disclosed. Kevin Bright was never charged with possessing any drugs found at his sisters home. <BR>The day before the Otero murders a plane crashed in Miami that was believed to have been in route to Wichita from Puerto Rico. The Otero&#39;s had recently arrived in Wichita from Puerto Rico and Mr. Otero was working at Cook Airfield in Rose Hill.  <BR>Kevin Bright has the almost unbelievable good furtune of wrestling the gun away from his attacker as he is being bound and then the equally almost unbelievable misfortune of turning the gun on the intruder and having the gun misfire not once but twice as Bright points the gun at the intruders stomach. The odds of having both these things happen are almost astronomical. Bright is then shot twice but escapes and flags down a motorist and passanger and thell them &#34;I&#39;ve been shot. There&#39;s a guy in the house doing a job on my sister.&#34; Not some guy shot me and he&#39;s in the house trying to kill my sister. He&#39;s &#34;doing a job on my sister.&#34; Who talks like that? That sounds like a line out of a mob movie or something. <BR>Kevin Bright no longer lives in Wichita and is a born-again Christian. <BR>What happened to Michael L Williams I don&#39;t know. It is interesting to note that although no relation a potential BTK victim had the last name of Williams. <BR>Katheryn Bright and the Otero&#39;s are dead. <BR>BTK has never claimed Katheryn Bright as one of his victims. <BR>Isn&#39;t all of this very strange? All of the above has been dismissed as coincidences and no connections.  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3981-->
<!--Post: 3983--><!--Time: 1105500594-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3983"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 7:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->He did call or refer to Anna Williams #8 did he not? That doesn&#39;t mean Kathryn Bright was one of the 7.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3983-->
<!--Post: 3986--><!--Time: 1105501104-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3986"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 7:38 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Johno <BR> <BR>Excelent post, great thinking, and yes I agree , lots of strange coincidences! hmmm... <BR> <BR>skov<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3986-->
<!--Post: 3989--><!--Time: 1105502678-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3989"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Wade<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wade<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 8:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe that Kevin never really wrestled the gun away OR tried to get off 2 shots.  When you say, Johno, that the odds of this are astronomical you&#39;re right.  I think he made this up &#40;as young men do&#41; to make it look like he had gotten an upper hand on the intruder just to make himself look tough.  Not meaning to offend K.B.  I just don&#39;t think it happened.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3989-->
<!--Post: 3996--><!--Time: 1105508179-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3996"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 9:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->To be accurate we have to say that Kathryn Bright was never claimed by btk AS FAR AS WE KNOW. I mention this as at least some police seem to include her and the authorities have never said she was NOT a btk victim.  The way the police are keeping so many things secret they may have a reason to believe she is a btk victim.  Notice that if her brother had not been with her the crime might very well have looked very very similar to the Vian, Fox, and Wegerle killings.  My guess, and that&#39;s all, is that this is btk.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3996-->
<!--Post: 4006--><!--Time: 1105529783-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4006"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 3:36 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This may be something, I don&#39;t know. <b>A long-term Wichita resident</b> will need to verify some  information. <i>If</i> everything adds up, it&#39;s another nudge in the direction of the Bright attack being perpetrated by BTK. I&#39;ve read that Murdock Park may be in an area with a sizeable African-American population. Is this correct? If  correct, that&#39;s part one. Next, the area of the Bright attack. According to what just I read the Bright residence, in 1974, was located in a &#34;notably&#34; African-American neighborhood. Is this accurate? If so, then it&#39;s possible that BTK, whom I believe to be white, was either unaffected by the presence of African-Americans &#40;or anyone else&#41; or possibly had black friends although they obviously didn&#39;t live near the Brights. Please remember that this is 1974 we&#39;re talking about, things weren&#39;t the same with race relations then as now. Also, this was presented &#40;Brights living in a largely African-American community, and no other BTK victims did&#41; <BR>as a significant reason why some don&#39;t consider the Bright attack a BTK crime. <BR> <BR>If Murdock Park is considered a largely black place and BTK was willing to drop the package there, late at night, I&#39;d say that this demonstrates that BTK may have been more willing to carry out the Bright attack, even if the Brights were living in a neighborhood where blacks also lived. <BR> <BR>Can a Wichitan determine if Murdock Park meets the above demographic criteria, ethnic-wise, and even more important, can it be determined that in 1974, the Brights resided in a similarly ethnic area? Even if this can be shown, it&#39;s hardly conclusive but certainly interesting and, I think, helps the case of the Brights as BTK victims a little more. My own belief is that the Bright attack was always a BTK crime. This will be a long post, but this idea is worth examining if the information is accurate. <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4006-->
<!--Post: 4009--><!--Time: 1105533542-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4009"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 4:39 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I meant to add that the other reason the Bright attack was/is not considered by some a BTK attack <BR>is that BTK failed to control the situation when compared with the evil brio he so deftly demonstrated at the Otero household. I understand this argument, but consider it weak, perhaps even negligible after Kevin Bright&#39;s interview and after thinking things over in general. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4009-->
<!--Post: 4016--><!--Time: 1105538403-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4016"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Beck<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Beck<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 6:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think that Kathryn was a BTK victim. Keep in mind I&#39;ve only just started learning more about this case, so I really could be wrong.  <BR> <BR>First off, I realize that there is no known letter, poem, whatever from BTK claiming her. But remember he has made it a point to make sure people know what he&#39;s done, for example, with the Otero murders, didn&#39;t he send a letter to WPD to say that the three men that turned themselves in, did not do it, that he did? And what about the letter he sent to the Fager &#40;sp?&#41; household? He said he didn&#39;t do that one. He&#39;s obviously proud of his work. He wouldn&#39;t want someone else to claim his work and he wouldn&#39;t want something that he didn&#39;t do to be connected to him with labels like &#34;definite BTK victim&#34; attached to it unless he did do it. He did claim 8 victims, so I just think that he doesn&#39;t want to come out and say that Kathryn was number 5 because of how everything went down, but at the same time, he&#39;s never corrected anyone &#40;that we know of&#41; to say that her murder wasn&#39;t his doing.  <BR> <BR>And second off, I think that he does have a &#34;signature&#34; that he&#39;s left at each scene. I&#39;m not talking about the cut phone lines, or the half naked victims, I think there is something else that only the WPD knows about. More than likely it&#39;s something that they keep secret to know when the communications are really coming from BTK. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4016-->
<!--Post: 4030--><!--Time: 1105552158-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4030"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 9:49 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Beck, as you say, the way things went down may have made him squeamish. I get the impression the Bright attack has always been considered by a majority to be a BTK crime. Couple what is probably a perception of failure on BTK&#39;s part with the majority belief that he did the Brights, and maybe that&#39;s enough for him. Not that he&#39;s happy about it, but it&#39;ll do, he can rationalize it. Hard to say. I&#39;ll try to condense my above, confusing &#40;to me&#41; post: <BR> <BR><i>IF</i> it&#39;s true that the Murdock Park area and the Bright residence were both sites with a large African-American presence, I think one of the two reasons for the Bright-isn&#39;t-BTK argument is ever more weakened. <BR>The Bright-isn&#39;t-BTK argument is: 1. BTK didn&#39;t control the Brights as he had controlled the Oteros. 2. The Brights were the only BTK victims living in an area with a clearly visible black presence. <BR> <BR>Reason one is flimsy, as BTK was surprised and Reason two is less significant because a much older BTK had no qualms about walking through a largely black area in the wee hours to make a drop. Would it then not follow that a far younger BTK, in 1974, perhaps at his highest level of confidence and being cocky anyway, would have few or no qualms about attacking in a largely black neighborhood? It doesn&#39;t definitely follow but is a decent possibility, further undermining the ethnic argument which is used by BTK-did-Bright doubters. BTK attacked the Brights, I&#39;m convinced. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4030-->
<!--Post: 4410--><!--Time: 1106331970-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4410"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jrl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 10:26 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I question whether Ms. Bright was a victim.  No semen at the crime scene.  That is his purpose.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
