<!--Post: 4954--><!--Time: 1106838892-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4954"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 7:14 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->You don&#39;t need a numerology guide or word jumble software to see it...The police never believed the two crimes were connected until 1978...It is a fact that Julie Otero and Kathryn worked side by side... <BR> <BR>Julie Otero, according to Charlie, was a lady that liked to help people...I am sure at a minimium she talked extensively with the 21 y/o Kathryn.  I have managed similar businesses and have seen how these relationships are formed by co-workers.  It&#39;s not like the work was exciting.  Kathryn was a cute young girl working with them that the older ladies would have taken an interest in. Ladies talk and share all sorts of stuff...They would have eaten lunch together in the factory breakroom...I can hear Julie talking about her husband Joe and personal life...I would not be surprised to find out they even socialized after work and spoke on the phone.  Charlie might or might not even know or remember. <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t think BTK even worked at Coleman, but his friends the Brights did.  The Brights also knew Mike Williams, thier 26 y/o supervisor who was shot on January 12, 1974.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
