<!--Post: 5533--><!--Time: 1107177625-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5533"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 5:20 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey yall, I&#39;m still looking for Kathrine&#39;s middle name. I think it could be as simple as that. He said BTK will be on the next vicitm. Maybe it was her name that got her targeted. This would mean he stalked her and some how got her middle name. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5533-->
<!--Post: 5535--><!--Time: 1107180802-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5535"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Essevi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Essevi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 6:13 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nugzter- According to the &#34;Midwest Historical and Genealogical Society&#34;, Kathryn&#39;s middle initial is &#34;D&#34;. &#40;It&#39;s a start anyway&#41; <BR> <a href="http://skyways.lib.ks.us/kansas/genweb/mhgs/74obits.htm" target=_top>http://skyways.lib.ks.us/kansas/genweb/mhgs/74obit s.htm</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5535-->
<!--Post: 5549--><!--Time: 1107188237-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5549"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Analyzer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Analyzer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 8:17 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->After looking over the timeline again I believe it is evident that the Bright killing isn&#39;t BTK related. <BR> <BR>His letter of October 1974  <BR> <BR>&#34;In October of 1974, just nine months after the Otero family murders, the Wichita Eagle&#39;s Don Granger received an anonymous call, presumably from the Otero killer himself. The caller directed him to a mechanical engineering textbook in the Wichita Public Library. Inside the book, Granger found a letter claiming credit for the killings of the Joseph Otero family, and promising more victims.&#34; <BR> <BR>only claims the Otero murder with no reference to the Bright killing which occured on April 4, 1974. <BR> <BR>Based on how much he wants credit for the other murders I&#39;m positive that he would have also claimed credit for the Bright murder in that original letter. <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5549-->
<!--Post: 5558--><!--Time: 1107191651-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5558"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 9:14 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If you take BTK&#39;s words at face value &#40;?&#41;, that would be correct.  However, here are some theories as to why he may not want to mention Bright: <BR> <BR>If you take Kevin Bright&#39;s recollection at face value: <BR>- It was an embarrassing disaster, nothing went right, and he damn near got killed. <BR>- Linking the crimes might given WPD enough clues to have pointed in his direction. <BR> <BR>If you do not take Kevin Bright&#39;s recollection at face value: <BR>- If Kevin knew the person known as BTK, the BTK moniker, besides standing for bind torture, and kill, could also be used as an inside message to constantly threaten Kevin with what was at stake for ID&#39;ing the person we know as BTK. Example: BTK = Bright, Thomas, Kevin. <BR>- If they linked the two crimes, they would look for connections.  They would look much harder for a Coleman connection, look at each players personal relationships, etc.  It might make them more skeptical of Kevin&#39;s story. Can you imagine how high profile the Bright investigation would have become?  Many more resources would have been brought to bear.  Had this been done at the time, I feel there is a high probability the crimes would have been solved. <BR> <BR>Provided this was a BTK crime, and the police have more info than we do and they now feel it is, the letter successfully confused the WPD investigation.  There had to be rumors going around.  The letter set-up the Otero&#39;s as a random serial killer crime with no other motivation, despite the fact Joe Otero was extremely afraid in advance for his families safety.???  And, by not connecting with the Bright&#39;s, with no other explanation, it validated Kevin&#39;s story as a crime committed by a stranger. While BTK wanted credit, at the time, he didn&#39;t want to be caught.  The letter may turn out to be the most brilliant thing he ever did. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5558-->
<!--Post: 5564--><!--Time: 1107195037-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5564"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 10:10 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK waited 18 years to claim responsibility for murdering Vicki Wegerle... As far as we know he never claimed to have killed Miss Bright. <BR> <BR>He does know that Kathryn Bright is counted in the total victims known count by just about everyone and has not disputed the # total... at least as far as we know.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5564-->
<!--Post: 5605--><!--Time: 1107216282-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5605"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 4:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;Do the cop think that all those deaths are not related? Yes, the M.O. is different in each, but look at the pattern that is developing. The victims are tie up _ most have been women _ phone cut _ bring some bondage mater sadist tendencies _ no struggle, outside the death spot _ no wntness except the Vian&#39;s kids. <BR> <BR>You guess the motive and the victims.&#34; <BR> <BR>BTK - 1978 <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5605-->
<!--Post: 6260--><!--Time: 1107642114-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6260"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 2:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Interesting that Susan Peters, the news lady who has read all of BTK&#39;s info sent to KAKE and spoke with Kevin Bright last year, said in an interview Vian was the 5th person killed by BTK...the only evidence would be BTK saying he didn&#39;t and maybe perhaps saying who number 7 was...or she misspoke...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6260-->
<!--Post: 6274--><!--Time: 1107647608-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6274"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Msrusty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Msrusty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 3:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I noticed this too. What came to my mind was maybe she wasn&#39;t counting the Otero children. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6274-->
<!--Post: 7181--><!--Time: 1108262600-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7181"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Msrusty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Msrusty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 6:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;ve been doing more reading on the Otero and Bright cases and I think I&#39;m more convinced that Bright was not BTK related. The reason I&#39;m having difficulty beleiving it was BTK is the fact that he was able to control all 4 Oteros but yet had trouble with Kevin Bright. I would think IF he had done the Bright killing he would have claimed it. He could have done it at the time he claimed Otero&#39;s. I would think he&#39;d have written a poem about how he wasn&#39;t able to do what he wanted to do thanks to Kevin getting away. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7181-->
<!--Post: 7185--><!--Time: 1108264465-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7185"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 7:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Msrusty - I understand what you&#39;re saying. But your point about BTK wanting to &#34;write&#34; about a failure goes against what I think is generally known about a psychopathic liar with a narcissistic ego - he would definitely want to put that out-of-control fiasco behind him. IMO, he wouldn&#39;t want to be associated with something that spiraled out of his control. <BR> <BR>His twisted and stupid thinking is all about &#34;him&#34; and his &#34;perfection&#34; &#40;what an idiot!&#41;. Any association with something gone wrong is outside of his self-absorbed little mind.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7185-->
<!--Post: 7189--><!--Time: 1108267687-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7189"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 8:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Maybe the reason why BTK didn´t have the same control over the Bright´s was because there were no children in the house.  <BR>I belive that BTK used threats to the children present in the house, in the other murders to keep control over the victims &#40;except Nancy Fox who had no problem with due to her beeing one woman&#41;parents would do ANYTHING to protect their children,and IMO thats exactly what BTK knew and used as a tactic.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7189-->
<!--Post: 7219--><!--Time: 1108293538-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7219"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Suspiria_2<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Suspiria_2<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 3:18 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->if this is his crime, my opinion is that he would never admit to it.  lillymarie has some pretty good reasons, but i believe his main one for &#34;failing to mention&#34; might just be self-preservation.  he left a LIVE victim at the scene, and if claimed, everyone would know that Kevin Bright saw the actual BTK, instead of merely suspecting that he did so. <BR> <BR>How many statements did Kevin Bright make to the police?  if they know that he saw the actual BTK, i doubt that his phone number and/or whereabouts would ever be unknown to wichita police.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7219-->
<!--Post: 7228--><!--Time: 1108313422-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7228"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Msrusty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Msrusty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 8:50 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I do understand how having the kids around might have enabled BTK to better control the situation at the Otero&#39;s. Parents would do anything BTK wanted in order to protect the kids. But I&#39;m still not totally convinced it is related. I think BTK could find it in his mind to claim Bright without admitting failure.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7228-->
<!--Post: 7236--><!--Time: 1108315899-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7236"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 9:31 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Good point Suspiria, not taking credit for Bright leaves all of Kevin&#39;s eye-witness accounts of his appearance, age, height, etc. in question.  <BR> <BR>And if he didn&#39;t do the Bright crime, then it is to his advantage not to say so...for the very same reason.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7236-->
<!--Post: 7274--><!--Time: 1108349185-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7274"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 6:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I wouldn&#39;t put much weight into anything Kevin said to the police back then. Not because of his two superficial wounds to the head, but because a large amount of heavy drugs was found in the home when police searched it after Kathryn&#39;s murder.  <BR> <BR>As the story goes, he and his sister went to get a loan that day, supposedly to buy a motorcycle. He had been out of work for a while, she was working, she was going to be co-signer. They returned home to find the man aiming the gun at them.... and so on... <BR> <BR>Kevin was living with his parents in Valley Center at the time of his sister&#39;s murder. So, did the drugs found in the home belong to him, or to Kathryn? <BR> <BR>Was Kathryn involved in drug dealing? She didn&#39;t seem the type, she had a job. <BR> <BR>This is just one reason to ponder on.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7274-->
